  "description": "Erection of a replacement single storey rear extension and installation of a roof light to the two storey rear outrigger to the house and installation of a replacement front and side boundary close board fence with two front close board pedestrian gates to the house's front garden.  ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications:  P-119 (Rev D) Received: 31 July 2026,  P-110 (Rev D), P-120 (Rev D) Received: 30 July 2026,  P-111 (Rev A), P-117 (Rev C) Received: 29 July 2026,  P-116 (Rev B) Received: 12 June 2026,  P-112, P-113 (Rev A), P-114 (Rev A), P-115, P-118 (Rev A), TQRQM26072144214710 Received: 30 April 2026,  Unreferenced Location Plan Received: 07 April 2026.  \r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.  ",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the single storey rear extension to the house hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing house, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed replacement front boundary treatment to the house's front garden shall comprise a timber close board fence and gates only and be permanently retained as such.  \r\n\r\nReasons:  To protect the character and historic integrity of the site and Bedford Park Conservation Area.  ",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the side and rear elevations, and roof, of the development hereby permitted.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy."
  ],
